  "explanation": {
    "md_es": [
      "**ever / never**",
      "",
      "- **Have you ever + participio …?** (preguntas, 'alguna vez') → *Have you ever climbed a mountain?*",
      "- **I've never + participio** (nunca; ya es negativa, no se usa *not*) → *I've never been to Italy.*",
      "- Con **not … ever** también: *I haven't ever been to Italy.* (menos frecuente)",
      "",
      "**Cuántas veces:** *once (1) · twice (2) · three times (3) · four times (4)…* — *How many times have you been to Spain?*",
      "",
      "**Superlativo + ever:** *It's the best film I've ever seen.* · *She's the nicest person I've ever met.* (se usa present perfect después del superlativo).",
      "",
      "**Ojo:** no se dice *haven't never* (doble negación). Y *never* va entre *have* y el participio.",
      "",
      "Pronunciación: *climb* /klaɪm/ (la b es muda) · *once* /wʌns/ · *twice* /twaɪs/."
    ],
    "common_mistakes_es": [
      {
        "wrong": "I haven't never been there.",
        "right": "I've never been there.",
        "note": "No se usa doble negación."
      },
      {
        "wrong": "I've been two times.",
        "right": "I've been twice.",
        "note": "Dos veces = twice."
      }
    ],
    "false_friends": []
  },
